me{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{15{sin}^{2}⁡t+({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{15{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\frac{4y}{x},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{4y}{x} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{4y}{x}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\sqrt{15{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535170 true] [17592186335206 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335207 13194139535170 true] [17592186335206 1089 "q-123145" 13194139535170 true] [17592186335206 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535170 true] [17592186335206 1100 "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}3y\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the ellipse $49{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=49,$ traversed once in the counterclockwise direction?" 13194139535170 true] [17592186335206 1113 #uuid "02cef69c-cbb8-55b1-bcf6-b14618446fe6" 13194139535170 true] [17592186335206 1145 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{7}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $1$ and $7,$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+7\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(7\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+49{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{48{cos}^{2}⁡t+({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{48{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=3y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =3(7\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=21\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}3y\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }21\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\sqrt{48{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =21{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\sqrt{48{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535170 true] [17592186335207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335208 13194139535170 true] [17592186335207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335209 13194139535170 true] [17592186335207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335210 13194139535170 true] [17592186335207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335211 13194139535170 true] [17592186335207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335212 13194139535170 true] [17592186335207 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535170 true] [17592186335207 1041 "selection" 13194139535170 true] [17592186335207 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335208 13194139535170 true] [17592186335207 1110 #uuid "a5ba98b8-bb2f-5eab-bd50-bbab73e0df84" 13194139535170 true] [17592186335208 1034 "21{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\sqrt{48{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139535170 true] [17592186335208 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535170 true] [17592186335208 1111 #uuid "b2bbb547-74c1-5756-857c-0b5a51e13fe6" 13194139535170 true] [17592186335209 1034 "21{\\int }_{0}^{