t)=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12{sin}^{2}⁡t+4({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12{sin}^{2}⁡t+4} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=2x,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}2x\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =16{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{3{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535170 true] [17592186335214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335215 13194139535170 true] [17592186335214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335216 13194139535170 true] [17592186335214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335217 13194139535170 true] [17592186335214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335218 13194139535170 true] [17592186335214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335219 13194139535170 true] [17592186335214 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535170 true] [17592186335214 1041 "selection" 13194139535170 true] [17592186335214 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335215 13194139535170 true] [17592186335214 1110 #uuid "361bbc11-5a63-5de1-8be9-0480c5d7a02a" 13194139535170 true] [17592186335215 1034 "16{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{3{sin