ame{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8{sin}^{2}⁡t+({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+8{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=16xy$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =16\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡t=48\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}16xy\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }48\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\sqrt{1+8{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =48{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{1+8{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=1+8{sin}^{2}⁡t,$ $\\text{d}u=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}48{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{1+8{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{9}^{1}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}{|}_{9}^{1} \\\\  & =2({1}^{3/2}-{9}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =2(1-27) \\\\  & =-52\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535170 true] [17592186335242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335243 13194139535170 true] [17592186335242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335244 13194139535170 true] [17592186335242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335245 13194139535170 true] [17592186335242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335246 13194139535170 true] [17592186335242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335247 13194139535170 true] [17592186335242 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535170 true] [17592186335242 1041 "selection" 13194139535170 true] [17592186335242 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335243 13194139535170 true] [17592186335242 1110 